<u>03-SEP-2005 10:59 PM (AUS Time)</u><br>
Today, M and I slept in just a little late.  Our plan today was simple, we would check out the Tjapakai Aboriginal Center (pronounced JAB-A-GUY).  It was really the only thing we were going to have time for as the other options would take a few hours of driving and we only had about 4 hours before the sun set.
<p>
We drove out to Tjapakai and learned about the history of the Aboriginese.  What I found interesting was their creation story.  They believed a man was all alone in the world and one day his calf starting feeling funny and got swollen up very big. And out of this swollen calf, a baby boy was born.  The man left the baby to go get it some food but in the mean time, a woman from the sky came down and breast fed it.  She would continue to come down and feed the baby.  The baby grew very quickly from a boy to a man and then one day the woman stopped coming. The man called out for the woman and she finally came. They went up into the sky together and got married.  Out of their marriage came two brothers, one good and one evil.  One would make it hard for people to survive in an attempt to not make them lazy, the other would help the people.  The evil brother would created manhunting crocs and large mountains while the good brother would guide the people who were lost.  The brothers would fight all the time and that is how many of the animals and landscape was formed.
<p>
<!--
<img src=http://www.mybigadventure.com/ankesh/picupload/Uploads/Images/1126437918_1.jpg>-->
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=../picupload/Uploads/Images/1126437918_1.jpg"><img src="picupload/Uploads/Images/Small/1126437918_1.jpg"></a>
<p>
We also got to see traditional dances, get a lesson on medicinal herbs/plants, get a lesson on a digeradoo (sp?) playing, and learn how to throw a spear and boomerang.  In the end, we saw a movie giving the history of Aboriginese in Australia and the white man's conquest of them.  All in all, a fun time. 
<p>
<!--
<img src=http://www.mybigadventure.com/ankesh/picupload/Uploads/Images/1126437918_2.jpg>-->
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=../picupload/Uploads/Images/1126437918_2.jpg"><img src="picupload/Uploads/Images/Small/1126437918_2.jpg"></a>
