<img src=http://www.mybigadventure.com/ankesh/picupload/Uploads/Images/1126437918_3.jpg>-->
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=../picupload/Uploads/Images/1126437918_3.jpg"><img src="picupload/Uploads/Images/Small/1126437918_3.jpg"></a>
<p>
It was a Saturday, so I decided to go check out the night life in Cairns.  Cairns is a backpackers paradise.  The town is just setup that way.  Tons of hostels, hotels, tour operators, souvenir shops, and of course bars.  And after the young kids are done diving or skydiving or bungy jumping, they are charged full of adrenaline and money in hand to do some good old fashion drinking.  They even dress the part. Guys in their clubby shirts and jeans, women in their dresses and heels.  Night life, just like in any other big town in America.  But things to quiet down by midnight because people have to get up early the next day to catch a dive or tour.  So if you come here, expect it to be somewhat of a college town. I didn't mind.  I decided to partake in a beer myself.  Here, contrary to popular opinion, I did not see a single can of Fosters.  Here, I see XXXX lager which is the name of their beer.  And their slogan --"Our Beer."  But noone drinks in excess, no puking, noone getting hostile, etc.
<p>
Tomorrow I will be doing two dives off the Reef.  We'll be going via a fast catamaran.  Should be a blast. Cheers.  Oh yeah, 3 of the most common phrases around here are "G'day, Mate, and No Worries."  Gotta love these Aussies, they are so nice.
<p>
